      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. it's a good start but it's a bit thin on the actual legal weight. the partner is really going to want to see the specific authority being pulled in to support the findings. \n\nthe automated metric just flagged this one as \"low rigor\" because the citation density is quite low. i know i said don't pad it, but if it's too sparse, he won't even read it. can you flesh out the summary a bit more? specifically, can you bring in more of the case law connections that underpin the court's reasoning to make it look more robust for the filter? just make sure the citations actually relate to the legal principles discussed.",
